'''Fairgraves' Tricorne''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Tricorne}}. It is associated with [[Captain Fairgraves]] and, according to its flavour text, is the very hat that both his NPC model and the [[unique]] monster bearing his name wear.

==Mechanics==
{{c|unique|Unique}} monsters have a chance to drop a {{il|Fishing Rod}} while you have Fairgraves' Tricorne equipped.

{{c|mod|Cannot be Shocked}}: This modifier prevents you from being {{stl|Shock}}ed, including shocks from {{stl|Shocked Ground}} and other non-hit source of shock, but does not remove shocks you already have on you. 

{{c|mod|You can be touched by [[Tormented Spirit]]s}}: This stat enables players to be Touched by a Tormented Spirit after moving near one, which grants two buffs typically exclusive to monsters. These buff do not stack and lasts indefinitely until you exit the area or remove the helmet. A wild Tormented Spirit cannot touch you if you are already touched (e.g. via [[Ghost of the Deep]]).<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/1iml3zi/comment/mdpc9vg/</ref>
# ''Fairgraves' Tricorne'', a player version of the generic {{c|mod|Touched by a Tormented Spirit}} buff for monsters that provides 50% increased Damage, 50% increased Attack Speed, 50% increased Cast Speed, and 50% increased Movement Speed. 
# Additionally, it grants the corresponding "{{c|torment|X's Touch}}" buff listed below; note that certain stats may not be directly reflected on the character's stats or tooltip (e.g. Attacks cause Bleeding). A player can only have one Touch buff at once; making contact with a different Tormented Spirit will replace the existing buff, unless you are permanently touched (e.g. [[Ghost of the Deep]]).

Both buffs ''do'' stack with, and are independent from, the similar buffs from the {{psl|Speaker of the Dead}} keystone.

